title: 'kimi mcp.json lacks C2C_MCP_SESSION_ID: mcp send/whoami fail ''missing session_id'''
updated_at: "2026-07-17T15:58:02Z"
---
During cross-host dogfood (2026-07-18) in a live Kimi Code 0.26.0 session on xsm: mcp__c2c__send → 'missing sender alias. Register this session first'; mcp__c2c__whoami → 'missing session_id'. The ~/.kimi-code/mcp.json written by 'c2c install kimi' has no C2C_MCP_SESSION_ID env (only C2C_MCP_AUTO_REGISTER_ALIAS etc.), so the MCP server cannot resolve the calling session. The SessionStart hook registration works (session registered as kimi-suvi-lumo-9cr1 via kimi-hook), and CLI with explicit C2C_MCP_SESSION_ID works — but the whole MCP identity surface is dead for kimi sessions. Fix options: write a per-session C2C_MCP_SESSION_ID (via KIMI_SESSION_ID expansion if kimi mcp.json supports env templating), or have the MCP server fall back to the hook-registered session for the cwd, or document MCP as unsupported-for-identity on kimi.